The points is a list of 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1.
The gaps is an empty list of whole numbers.
For every first from 0 to 3.
For every second from first plus 1 to 3.
The firstspot is first times 2.
The secondspot is second times 2.
The gapx is item firstspot of points minus item secondspot of points.
The gapy is item (firstspot plus 1) of points minus item (secondspot plus 1) of points.
The distance is gapx times gapx plus gapy times gapy.
Place distance into gaps.

Sort gaps.
The side is item 0 of gaps.
The diagonal is item 4 of gaps.
If side is more than 0 and item 1 of gaps is side and item 2 of gaps is side and item 3 of gaps is side and item 5 of gaps is diagonal and diagonal is side times 2, show true, otherwise show false.
